                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "GOOD GOD. Looking at the trailer (which literally said \"an relax vr experience,\" I laughed), I got this game essentially assuming it would be terrible.  IT WAS WORSE THAN I THOUGHT. This is literally less fun than the app.  It's actually horrific and unbelievable how bad it was. \nWhy the hell would you make a paper toss game for VR, where [b] YOU DON'T EVEN \"TOSS\" ANYTHING. You literally aim your controller and hold down a power meter. [/b] This mechanic is implemented in non-vr apps because you can't simulate the physics of throwing. In VR, it's totally possible! It's inconceivable that the morons who made this cash grab literally didn't even add the ability to \"throw.\"\n\nBut wait, it gets even worse! You are forced to use two controllers. Why?? Because you have to hold down the power meter using your non-dominant hand's trigger, while aiming using your dominant hand. How is it even legal to willingly break the game this badly?\nThe game is even glitched, horribly.  If you don't aim through a specific hitbox on the trash can, the paper will just clip right through it. WTF. \nNot only is this worthless garbage not worth one dollar, it's not even worth playing for free. You would literally have to pay me to play this trash. \n\nI'm convinced that the other wads of paper in the trash can you're tossing balls into, would have information worth 10x more than the game itself. \n\nThe developers should be ashamed of themselves. Seriously.",
